{"timestamp":"2026-09-02T09:41:32.318Z","ordinal":17535,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a05669-fc4c-7aa0-b9a1-034d833ed8ed","turn_id":"01a0617d-e48f-7d23-abaf-7046ea0b2276","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-dcac6635-5e0c-412b-b1d7-9bf676aaa850","process_id":"26358","command":["/bin/bash","-lc","sed -n '280,560p' /lambda/nfs/whchoi/experiment-results/cd3-20260901-route/CD3_OPTIMIZATION_AND_P4FLAT_COMPARISON.md"],"cwd":"file:///home/ubuntu","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '280,560p' /lambda/nfs/whchoi/experiment-results/cd3-20260901-route/CD3_OPTIMIZATION_AND_P4FLAT_COMPARISON.md","name":"CD3_OPTIMIZATION_AND_P4FLAT_COMPARISON.md","path":"/lambda/nfs/whchoi/experiment-results/cd3-20260901-route/CD3_OPTIMIZATION_AND_P4FLAT_COMPARISON.md"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":"| Batch | P4 TTFT median | CD3 TTFT median | P4 TPOT median | CD3 TPOT median | CD3 TPOT change |\n|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|\n| 64 | 1846.63 ms | 1838.72 ms | 124.66 ms | 114.51 ms | 8.14% faster |\n| 128 | 337.96 ms | 338.02 ms | 180.59 ms | 166.64 ms | 7.72% faster |\n\nTPOT means were 129.95 versus 120.19 ms at batch 64 (7.51% faster) and\n196.80 versus 187.12 ms at batch 128 (4.92% faster). These are whole-engine\nresults, so they include weight routing, attention, scheduling, KV transport,\nKV decode, and CPU compression contention rather than isolating one codec\nkernel.\n\nFor a 16-layer KV-only pipeline, CD3's H2D/decode overlap reduced its own\nmakespan by 30.3% at N=256 and 25.8% at N=1024. Against P4Flat's best measured\nsetting, CD3 was 46.7%, 20.8%, and 1.0% faster at N=64/256/1024. The production\nthreshold keeps N<256 on one stream because two-stream event overhead exceeds\noverlap benefit there.\n\n## 9. Retained optimization work\n\n### 9.1 CPU encoder\n\n- Block-owner one-pass encoding: one OpenMP owner completes a KV block in\n  tile/thread/item order, eliminating global prefix buffers, barriers, and the\n  second source-exponent read.\n- Min/max exception-free fast path: if 16 exponents fit in one 3-bit range,\n  candidate search and per-element exception work are skipped.\n- Direct local Packed20x3 construction with uninitialized temporary exception\n  scratch; only valid entries are compacted.\n- NEON extraction of exponent/sign-mantissa and hierarchical packing of 16\n  three-bit codes.\n- SVE2 predicate counting only on the uncommon exception path.\n- CPU weight encoding by independent 64-row stripes, preserving the exact GPU\n  tile order while exposing enough parallel work.\n- Adaptive OpenMP team sizing and worker affinity, especially for an explicit\n  single KV worker.\n- Batched NumPy KV slot assignment instead of a per-block Python loop.\n- Weight encode defaults to CPU. GPU encode remains only behind the explicit\n  debug override `TIERED_SERVE_CD3_WEIGHT_CPU_ENCODE=0`.\n\n### 9.2 Standalone GPU decoder\n\n- Aligned two-`uint32` loading of each six-byte/48-bit code chunk. The final\n  thread reads bytes 1528..1535, so it never crosses a 1536-byte tile.\n- 128 physical threads per tile, each handling two logical 16-value chunks,\n  improving occupancy relative to the original 256-thread layout.\n- Two half-width live output accumulators followed by the same two 128-bit\n  stores, reducing register pressure. This improved aggregate layer-40 weight\n  decode by about 1.4%.\n- 2-D `(tile, block)` KV launch geometry.\n- Direct-to-final-cache indexed KV decode, eliminating the intermediate raw\n  BF16 copy.\n\n### 9.3 KV transport and orchestration\n\n- One aligned slot-major blob containing codes, sign/mantissa, bases, offsets,\n  and Packed20x3 entries, with explicit row strides in CPU/GPU kernels.\n- One `cudaMemcpyBatchAsync` submission for all selected K/V staging runs.\n- Selected-run staging for partial restores instead of copying every slot up\n  to the high-water mark.\n- Cached block/slot GPU metadata and one native paired K/V decode dispatch.\n- The loader publishes the canonical active set once per forward; per-layer\n  decoding then uses identity/version checks with generation-safe invalidation\n  instead of repeating a NumPy content comparison 80 times.\n- Dense steady-state plans that skip filtering, sorting, and contiguous-run\n  reconstruction.\n- Explicit-stream native decode dispatch and a two-slot compressed-blob HBM\n  ring overlap layer L+1 H2D with layer L decode for N>=256. Smaller restores\n  stay on one stream to avoid fixed event/stream overhead.\n- The KV memory planner accounts for CD3's fixed compressed row and reserves\n  one resident partial-tail row per request, preventing host over-allocation\n  and preserving full-block correctness.\n\n### 9.4 Fused Hopper kernel\n\n- Decode directly into WGMMA register A; no dense BF16 weight HBM write.\n- Expand each K tile's Packed20 exceptions into a shared exponent map before\n  WGMMA. This avoids P4Flat-style post-GEMM rank-1 correction for CD3's much\n  larger exception population.\n- Aligned two-`uint32` shared code extraction and register caching of each\n  48-bit code word rather than repeated byte loads.\n-